# build/core.aig -- the CORE-ONLY model (model A of the two-model split).
#
#   Hazard3 + the bus environment + the psgen properties.  No Sail model.
#
# Everything from `setattr` onwards is the same pass sequence as build_h3.ys /
# build_h3_fast.ys, applied to the same flat design, so build/core.aig is the
# same model as build/all.aig minus the (unconnected) specification instance.
#
# No `flatten` is needed: yosys-slang elaborates the whole hierarchy into a
# single `top` module, which is also why signals are named `cpu.core.foo`.
# build_h3_fast.ys's `flatten` exists only to merge in the separately-read
# build/spec.il, which this model does not have.
#
# HAZARD3_RTL and AHBL_SLAVE_ASSUMPTIONS_V are substituted by the Makefile.

# -DHAZARD3_RVFI_STANDALONE turns on hdl/hazard3_rvfi_monitor.vh, the core
# author's own definition of retirement, which gate 3's agreement assertion is
# stated against.  It is Hazard3's own switch for using the RVFI trace port
# outside the riscv-formal harness: hazard3_core.v:6-8 and
# hazard3_cpu_1port.v:10-12 then include hazard3_rvfi_standalone_defs.vh, which
# defines RISCV_FORMAL and the `RVFI_OUTPUTS / `RVFI_CONN port macros, so the
# harness supplies no boilerplate of its own.  It also removes the one
# non-synthesisable assert in the monitor (:329-332).  See check/h3_core_common.svh
# for the audit showing that it brings in no `assume` and no extra assertion.
read_slang --no-implicit-memories --top top -DSYNTHESIS -DYOSYS -DHAZARD3_RVFI_STANDALONE \
	check/h3_ahbl_master_props.sv \
	AHBL_SLAVE_ASSUMPTIONS_V \
	check/h3_core_top.sv \
	-F build/hazard3.scr \
	-I HAZARD3_RTL \
	--single-unit --no-proc

setattr -set keep 1 n:\\*
proc
global_clk \clk_i
opt_muxtree_2
opt_clean

memory_nordff
delete */t:$print
script h3_tieoff_undriven.ys
setundef -undriven -anyseq
memory_map -formal
delete -output
expose n:\\*

opt_muxtree_2
opt_expr
opt_dff
opt_clean
techmap
simplemap
dffunmap
opt_clean
stat
aigmap
write_aiger_2 -I -B -zinit -no-startoffset -ywmap build/core.ywmap -vmap build/core.vmap build/core.aig
